<article class="env-lemma" id="4257F4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/4257F4">Lemma <span data-tag="4257F4">7.1.3.13</span>.</a> Suppose that $U \subseteq X$ is paracompact, and let $\calU \subseteq \calB $ be a covering of $U$. Choose a linear ordering of $\calU $. Then the natural map $\pi : |N_{\calU }|_{X} \rightarrow U$ is a homotopy equivalence in $\Top _{/X}$. (In other words, there exists a section $s: U \rightarrow N_{\calU }$ of $\pi $, such that $s \circ \pi $ is fiberwise homotopic to the identity.) </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Any partition of unity subordinate to the open cover $\calU $ gives rise to a section of $\pi $. To check that $s \circ \pi $ is fiberwise homotopic to the identity, use a “straight line” homotopy. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>